  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Option 1:&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p><p>Cr&nbsp;is expected to have the highest second ionization enthalpy as after removal of&nbsp;4s&nbsp;electrons, the electrons will be removed from d-orbital.&nbsp;Cr+&nbsp;have stable half-filled d-orbital with maximum spin multiplicity.&nbsp;</p><p>Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></math></p><p>Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Co</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p>Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p>"
  }
